# Crewboard's projects, members and tasks policies, with each call run as the
# account that makes it. A Member that rewrites its own member row as Owner is
# refused, because the update is judged on the stored row too, where it is
# not an owner. The creator rule admits an Owner member insert only for a
# project whose row names the caller as created_by and that has no members,
# so create_project makes its caller the owner in one transaction and no
# other path does: not an outsider, not a Member, not a forged created_by,
# and not the creator once the project has members. An outsider's search
# and my_projects find nothing. The same lines print at O0, O1 and O2.
fixture: CrewboardRowPolicies.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step default: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = crewboard_row_policies.stdout.expected
step: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
step debug: built
exit: 0
stdout: == default
step release: jet run --release main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == default
